{
  "dom_id": "step-q210782",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{33}(2+x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{33}(2+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(\\frac{4}{33}t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{33})|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{33}+\\frac{4x}{33}-\\frac{12}{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{33}({x}^{2}+4x-12) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{33}(x+6)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{33}(x+6)(x-2), & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
